      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49289112",
      "score": 782,
      "comments": 409,
      "author": "thisisauserid",
      "published": "2026-08-13T17:23:22Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Google expands its Gemini API family, prioritizing high-speed, low-latency multimodal inference and cost-efficient token throughput.",
        "Available via Google AI Studio and Vertex AI, optimized for real-time developer workflows, structured outputs, and function calling.",
        "Delivers competitive reasoning and coding capabilities designed for scalable agentic applications without the compute overhead of flagship models."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "C3 0.8.3 Feature flags",
      "url": "https://c3-lang.org/blog/c3_0_8_3_feature_flags/",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/e9v9qi",
      "score": 7,
      "comments": 4,
      "author": "LowByteFox",
      "published": "2026-08-13T19:07:37Z",
      "bullets": [
        "C3 0.8.3 introduces native feature flags, enabling structured compile-time conditional compilation without relying on legacy C preprocessor macros.",
        "The mechanism provides granular control over modular builds, target architectures, and optional language extensions during compilation.",
        "Enhances build-time ergonomics and maintainability for systems programmers seeking modern C alternatives with full C ABI compatibility."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Unlocking _everything_ on the CPU with DRAM scrambling",
      "url": "https://github.com/xoreaxeaxeax/skitter-creek-bath-salts",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/a4zifd",
      "score": 37,
      "comments": 10,
      "author": "radex",
      "published": "2026-08-13T16:06:04Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Weak CPU DRAM scrambling implementations can be reverse-engineered, exposing plaintext memory to physical bus-sniffing and data-remanence attacks.",
        "Hardware DRAM scramblers mitigate signal integrity issues rather than providing cryptographic confidentiality like Intel TME or AMD SME.",
        "Bypassing DRAM scrambling enables physical adversaries to alter execution flows, compromise secure enclaves, and extract sensitive cryptographic keys."
      ]
    },
